KI-037 fix proposal (NOT APPLIED). Conditional: apply only after the owner's
decisive test (see ki-037-analysis.md section 6) shows the first photo is
correct with --async_shader_compilation=false or in a second session of the
same build. SDK hunks are against the pinned l34 SDK tree (a239b83) and would
ship like the other private SDK patches; paths are relative to the MCLA-R
repository root.

Idea: during the photo-capture window (guest freeze function sub_8263D120 ..
unfreeze sub_8263D1E0) the command processor waits for a pending pipeline
instead of silently dropping the draw. Normal gameplay keeps asynchronous
creation. Simply flipping async_shader_compilation at runtime is NOT safe:
draws for pipelines already queued on worker threads would be recorded with a
null PSO and replayed with the previous pipeline (deferred_command_list.cpp
kSetPipelineStateHandle ignores a null state).

